# Claims Module — API Endpoints, Validators & Hangfire Jobs

## API General Rules
- RESTful JSON; JWT Bearer auth (mock acceptable)
- Idempotency via `Idempotency-Key` header on all write operations
- **CorrelationId (BR-A-03):** `CorrelationIdMiddleware` reads `X-Correlation-Id` or generates a GUID; propagates via `ICorrelationIdAccessor` to all `IAuditLogService` writes in the same request
- All validation errors → HTTP 422 with structured error body (see 01-architecture.mdc)
- Swagger/OpenAPI must be accessible at deployed URL

## Non-FRS dev endpoints (Assessment §4.3 test credentials)

| Method | Route | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| POST | /api/auth/token | Mock JWT for `handler` / `supervisor` / `manager` — not in FRS §10; required for local/demo auth |

## Assessment API deviations (implement FRS, not Assessment)

- **Adjust reserve:** use `POST /api/claims/{id}/reserves` with `transactionType: Adjust` — do **not** add Assessment `PUT /api/claims/{id}/reserves/{reserveId}`

## Claims Endpoints
| Method | Route | MediatR Handler | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| POST | /api/claims | `CreateClaimCommand` | Full validation; atomic ClaimNumber; creates Claim + LossEvent + Parties + RiskObjects + optional reserve in ONE transaction; triggers ClaimCreated event; returns 201 with ClaimNumber |
| GET | /api/claims | `ListClaimsQuery` | Paginated. Filters: `status`, `dateFrom`, `dateTo`, `assignedHandlerId`, `causeOfLossCode`, `policyId`, `search`. `search` must match **claimNumber**, policyNumber, and clientName (FRS list). Returns: id, claimNumber, clientName, policyNumber, lossDate, status, totalReserves |
| GET | /api/claims/{id} | `GetClaimDetailQuery` | Full detail: parties, risk objects, reserve summary, doc list, recent audit entries |
| PUT | /api/claims/{id}/status | `TransitionClaimStatusCommand` | Body: `{ targetStatus, reason? }`. Validates state machine. HTTP 422 with blocking conditions if not permitted |
| GET | /api/claims/{id}/audit | `GetClaimAuditQuery` | Paginated, reverse-chronological, append-only |
| POST | /api/claims/{id}/parties | `AddClaimPartyCommand` | Logs `PARTY_ADDED` |
| DELETE | /api/claims/{id}/parties/{partyId} | `RemoveClaimPartyCommand` | Soft-remove (IsActive=false). HTTP 422 if removing last Claimant |
| POST | /api/claims/{id}/documents | `UploadClaimDocumentCommand` | Multipart form; store via IStorageService; max 50MB; allowed: PDF/JPEG/PNG/DOCX/XLSX/TXT/CSV; logs `DOCUMENT_UPLOADED` |
| GET | /api/claims/{id}/documents | `GetClaimDocumentsQuery` | Returns SAS URL (1-hour TTL) per document |

## Reserve Endpoints
| Method | Route | MediatR Handler | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| POST | /api/claims/{id}/reserves | `OpenReserveCommand` or `AdjustReserveCommand` | Body: `{ component, amount, changeReason, transactionType? }`. `Add` (default) opens component; `Adjust` adjusts existing. Creates ReserveHistory. If auto-approved → enqueue GL job. Returns 201 |
| GET | /api/claims/{id}/reserves | `GetClaimReservesQuery` | Summary (balance per component) + full transaction history |
| POST | /api/claims/{id}/reserves/{txnId}/approve | `ApproveReserveCommand` | Requires Supervisor or Manager role. Validate not self-approving. On success: status → Approved, enqueue GL job. Logs `RESERVE_APPROVED` |
| POST | /api/claims/{id}/reserves/{txnId}/reject | `RejectReserveCommand` | Requires Supervisor or Manager. Body: `{ rejectionReason }`. Status → Rejected. Logs `RESERVE_REJECTED` |
| POST | /api/claims/{id}/reserves/{txnId}/retract | `RetractReserveCommand` | Submitter only. Status → Cancelled. Logs `RESERVE_RETRACTED` |

